    what: "#997 (D-M8-18): an iesnium-headed pickaxe carrying both modifiers a spirit binding ritual can grant it at once -- necrotic at 3 (the afrit pentacle) and soulbound at 1 (the marid one), 3 modifier slots spent between them. forgeweave:modifiers stores id + level only, the same as every other modifier (ADR-0004 item 2), so a ritual-granted modifier needs no new component and no migration: nothing on this stack records that a ritual rather than the Tool Station put it there, and nothing needs to. granted_slots is 0 on purpose, which is the one thing that distinguishes this from a Draconic fusion upgrade's fixture -- a binding spends the slots its entries occupy (ModifierApplication#applyLevelSpendingSlots) rather than handing them back the way applyLevel does. Both modifiers keep working with compat.occultismRituals off, since both are reachable at the Tool Station too; the toggle only stops a new ritual from being performed."
